WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:03.480
<b>Fantasia</b>

3
00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.330
You listening, Pops?

4
00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.080
Saruyama brothers?

5
00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.370
I did it!

6
00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.580
[SHOJO]
Huh?

7
00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.750
[MASIRA gasps]

8
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.910
[LUFFY]
The City of Gold!

9
00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:28.970
It was right here!

10
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.780
That bonehead! He did it!

11
00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.240
[bell rings]

12
00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.200
Unbelievably beautiful.

13
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.370
Ah! That sound is amazing.

14
00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:49.660
What is it?

15
00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:56.210
It's come. As I always knew it would.

16
00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.800
– Destiny.
– [bell rings]

17
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.300
[SANJI]
Ah, this was the
ringing that Noland heard.

18
00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.600
Now I get it.

19
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.020
[PIERRE squawks]

20
00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:12.520
Singing. Listen.

21
00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.320
The Vearth is singing a song.

22
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.320
[SUU]
Ah.

23
00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.070
[bell rings]

24
00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:24.870
This is proof. God is real.

25
00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.750
[CHIEFTAIN]
This is surely a miracle!

26
00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:31.840
I had almost abandoned hope that we
would ever hear the golden bell again

27
00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:35.130
after nearly 400 years of silence.

28
00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:38.040
Great Warrior Kalgara.

29
00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.870
Can you hear it?

30
00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:45.540
The unmistakable echo
of the Fire of Shandora!

31
00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.250
[bell rings]

32
00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:51.170
Good heavens.

33
00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.560
What must've happened to this land?

34
00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.940
What is that strange chiming?

35
00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.430
The legendary bell?

36
00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.210
Could it be?

37
00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.240
[bell rings]

38
00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.450
[WYPER]
Montblanc Noland.

39
00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:11.600
Can you hear the bell sounding
from beyond your grave?

40
00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.730
May these chimes reverberate
all the way to your descendants.

41
00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.290
Now rest in peace, Noland.

42
00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.890
You like the bells ringing too?

43
00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.520
– [bell rings]
– Yeah, I bet you do.

44
00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.480
[SNAKE growls]

45
00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:48.290
[MASIRA]
Old man! This is it!

46
00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.850
[CRICKET]
Yeah! There's no doubt about it.

47
00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:55.900
Only one bell in this
world could echo so far!

48
00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:58.640
And with such emotion.

49
00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.130
Awesome!

50
00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:04.970
Absolutely!

51
00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:09.240
Y'know those giants you see
in the Cumuloregalis Clouds?

52
00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.240
The story goes a little
something like this.

53
00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:15.870
Whenever a human inhabits the sky
and the sun's rays shine upon him,

54
00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:20.420
his shadow is reflected on the deep mist,
and then cast far across the horizon.

55
00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:26.290
To onlookers, the shadow appears as if
it's a gigantic monster looming above.

56
00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.040
Ya mean those aren't really giants?

57
00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.750
They're actually somebody's shadow?

58
00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:32.250
That would mean we've already
found irrefutable proof

59
00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.290
that people do live in the sky!

60
00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:36.790
Am I right?

61
00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:39.500
Yeah, I once thought the story
was a meaningless fantasy

62
00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.090
and dismissed it altogether.

63
00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:45.380
But it seems there is
truth to this legend.

64
00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.510
[bell rings]

65
00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:48.640
My ears are filled
with the resounding cries

66
00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.820
of the golden bell.

67
00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.170
[CRICKET]
If a golden bell exists,

68
00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:59.240
then why not an entire city?

69
00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:03.420
Noland 
the Liar

70
00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.840
Noland was telling the truth!

71
00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.470
His reputation can finally be redeemed!

72
00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.720
Noland 
the Liar

73
00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:08.270
And with it, our family name!

74
00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:11.140
That's the reason you
rang the bell, isn't it, kid?

75
00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.350
Shrewd move!

76
00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.230
You have my thanks.

77
00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:16.820
I won't forget this.

78
00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:21.280
[CRICKET chuckles]

79
00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:28.030
<b>MONKEY</b>

80
00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:35.630
[CRICKET crying]

81
00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:37.460
– [SHOJO] What's wrong?
– [MASIRA] Hey, Cricket!

82
00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:39.490
Are you sick? Are you hurt?

83
00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:42.120
[CRICKET]
No, it's those kids.

84
00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.850
I'm just glad they're safe!

85
00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.270
[crying]

86
00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:50.730
I was... Guess I was just so worried!

87
00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:53.190
[BOTH laugh]

88
00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:10.760
Look! Up there!

89
00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:14.930
Hey, that's God's ship!

90
00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:26.780
He sunk!

91
00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.310
God Eneru and his ship are...

92
00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:33.450
[ISLANDER A]
...falling.

93
00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:43.750
[CHIEFTAIN]
The bell's ringing
ignites the Fire of Shandora,

94
00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:48.970
that long-gone city that took pride,
above all, in its prosperity.

95
00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:57.480
The reverberations serve as the island's
song, proclaiming the end of the battle.

96
00:07:57.480 --> 00:08:00.730
A melody longing to
be heard by the island

97
00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:05.520
and generations of its natives
and supporters for 400 years.

98
00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.830
[BIRDS call]

99
00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:17.040
[NARRATOR]
Although the
journey of this restless island

100
00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:22.890
seemed nearly endless, time cannot
fade even its most distant memory.

101
00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.720
For long ago, people entrusted their
words in the sound of the golden bell.

102
00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:36.570
Lacing each ring with
words of faith and hope,

103
00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.700
which resounded across the distant sea.

104
00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:43.880
[CRICKET]
My friends!

105
00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:51.300
[LUFFY]
It rang.

106
00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:57.760
Hey, I wonder if... if Pops heard it?

107
00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.720
[NAMI]
Yeah, I'm sure he did.

108
00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:11.490
[KALGARA]
We're right here!

109
00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.000
[ISLANDER A]
Bind the ropes
to the strongest-looking trees!

110
00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:47.200
[rustling]

111
00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:56.130
Aisa. Were you scared, dear?

112
00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:59.540
Surprise. Your treasure!

113
00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:01.880
So what? Who cares?

114
00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.680
Laki!

115
00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:13.480
[crying]

116
00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:16.070
[BRAHAM]
The others?

117
00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:18.070
[WARRIOR A]
They're fine! Don't try to speak.

118
00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:21.400
[WARRIOR B]
Who's that over there?

119
00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:24.730
[GENBOU]
Am I still alive?

120
00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.570
[CHOPPER]
No! You have to be treated right away!

121
00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:29.690
My wounds aren't that severe.

122
00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:32.900
Really. That guy.

123
00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.830
He needs help more than me.

124
00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.210
Look after him.

125
00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:47.770
[CHOPPER]
It's true!

126
00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:50.140
His body's worn out. He's dying!

127
00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:52.660
Yeah, but he was tryin' to kill us.

128
00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:54.510
We don't owe him anything.

129
00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:55.670
[ZORO]
I know.

130
00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.940
He was going all out,
just like the rest of us.

131
00:10:57.860 --> 00:10:59.650
It doesn't make much sense, but...

132
00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:04.910
Uh... He's a hero? Seriously?

133
00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:05.980
[ZORO sighs]
Who knows.

134
00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:08.900
[AISA]
Um...

135
00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.670
Help him, Raccoon-Doggy?

136
00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:14.460
[CHOPPER]
I'm a reindeer! Antlers! See?

137
00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:15.670
[sighs]

138
00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:18.840
Don't worry. He'll survive.

139
00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:20.260
[AISA]
Thanks, reindeer!

140
00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:27.140
[GAN FALL]
Pierre, you're
going to over-exert yourself.

141
00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:28.810
Go rest with the Blue Sea people.

142
00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:30.180
[PIERRE squawks]

143
00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:34.670
[GAN FALL]
Very well, then.

144
00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:37.550
I want you to go and
gather the families.

145
00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:40.300
[PIERRE squawks]

146
00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.700
[SANJI]
I guess anything's possible.

147
00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:46.580
Speaking of which, what do you think
happened to Eneru and the bell?

148
00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.710
Don't know I guess
they must've crashed.

149
00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:52.250
So we have a city of gold.

150
00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:54.230
But in name only.

151
00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:58.230
Which just means that our
adventure in poverty continues.

152
00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.820
I'd rather have dials
over gold any day.

153
00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.980
That's something we just
can't get from the Blue Sea.

154
00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:07.280
[SANJI]
I'm to the point where I'd
settle for some concrete news.

155
00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:08.980
I hope Nami's all right.

156
00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:10.690
And where's Conis?

157
00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:14.050
This not knowing is driving me crazy!

158
00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:17.470
[BRAHAM]
Do you think it's a good idea to leave
Wyper with the Blue Sea dwellers?

159
00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:19.300
[LAKI]
Don't worry, it'll be fine.

160
00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.580
It appears Aisa has befriended them.

161
00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:23.290
We'll just have to act quickly.

162
00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.540
If our enemy wakes before
we leave, we're finished.

163
00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:26.890
Gather those who can
move and we'll banish

164
00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.650
every last one of Eneru's
priests to the clouds.

165
00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:31.410
[GROUP]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

166
00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.070
So did you have a
chance to patch him up?

167
00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:37.640
[CHOPPER]
Yes. All he needs now is rest.

168
00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:39.180
[LUFFY]
Hey!

169
00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:47.740
[GROUP laughing]

170
00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.510
[SANJI]
Nami!

171
00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:51.380
Conis!

172
00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:52.880
[USOPP]
Luffy!

173
00:12:57.350 --> 00:13:00.520
We're back! I'm so glad you're okay!

174
00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:05.520
[CONIS]
I was afraid I wouldn't
see any of you again!

175
00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:08.020
[SANJI]
She was worried! Ah!

176
00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:09.110
Oh, please.

177
00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:10.860
I'm glad you guys grabbed some food.

178
00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:12.320
Where's it from?

179
00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:16.150
[NAMI]
We found the priests' storage locker
on our way back through the forest.

180
00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.440
There were lots more!

181
00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:20.310
But uh, how did you manage
to find your way back down?

182
00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:21.770
[LUFFY]
My Gum-Gum Balloon.

183
00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:25.270
[ZORO]
Conis, where's your old man?

184
00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:22.980
[USOPP]
Oh.

185
00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:28.820
He, um... Well, he...

186
00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.540
He protected me.

187
00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:31.920
And then Eneru...

188
00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.670
Don't tell me...

189
00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:44.320
I'm sorry.

190
00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.450
Yeah, me too.

191
00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:47.860
Me three.

192
00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.360
You're supposed to be dead!

193
00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:53.820
[PAGAYA]
Sorry, I'm alive!

194
00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:56.400
[CONIS]
Father!

195
00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:01.270
[NAMI]
You were on the lower
level of the White Sea?

196
00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:04.730
I found myself there after
being blasted from the ledge.

197
00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:06.410
And I wasn't alone.

198
00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:11.380
Countless others ended up in the same spot
while making their way toward Cloud End.

199
00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:17.080
Yet, as we speak, they too are now on the
journey back via the restored Milky Roads.

200
00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:19.910
Of course, given that there's
no longer an Angel Island,

201
00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:22.120
a new destination was chosen.

202
00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:23.450
Upper Yard.

203
00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.930
[GROUP laughing]

204
00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.770
Thank you so much.

205
00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.430
[HUSBAND]
We owe you our lives, god.

206
00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:39.800
Just Gan Fall.

207
00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:42.680
I no longer go by that title.

208
00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:45.060
You were all forced to work
in a place like this

209
00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:47.060
for six long years.

210
00:14:47.060 --> 00:14:48.150
I'm sorry.

211
00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:50.600
We lost Angel Island,

212
00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.850
the home we were supposed to return to.

213
00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:57.270
And like the Shandorians,
our birthright's now lost.

214
00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:00.070
Is the battle really over?

215
00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.970
God's army has gone,
but I just don't...

216
00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.220
My Chief.

217
00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:13.700
Do you really believe the 400-year
rift can be mended so easily?

218
00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:17.250
[USOPP]
Ah!

219
00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:19.410
Boy. I stuffed myself!

220
00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:20.920
Well, it's getting
pretty late you guys.

221
00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:22.630
It's time to hit the ship.

222
00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:24.960
Whoa, you're not talkin'
about leaving, are you?

223
00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:26.230
Relax.

224
00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.440
Usopp, can you believe
what she just said?

225
00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.150
Hardly. It's sick.

226
00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.490
I mean, the thought doesn't even cross
her mind to go out and look for gold.

227
00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.020
And she calls herself a pirate!

228
00:15:35.020 --> 00:15:38.190
[NAMI]
How'd you two like fat lips
to go with your fat bellies?

229
00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:46.240
It's time.

230
00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:49.500
And soon... I will return!

231
00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:53.080
To the wide-open sky:
the perfect home for a god!

232
00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:54.960
Pristine and unobstructed.

233
00:15:56.420 --> 00:16:00.670
Yes, and best of all,
no pests to get in my way!

234
00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:02.880
[laughing]

235
00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:05.180
I'll be sure no one gets near it.

236
00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:08.390
My own private paradise.

237
00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:11.320
A land boundless, exquisite.

238
00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:15.040
It's just like a dream...
which comes to life!

239
00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:19.860
Maxim.

240
00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:22.970
Set sail and deliver me to
my new floating kingdom,

241
00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:25.550
which shines brightly in the night.

242
00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:27.370
The land without end.

243
00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:29.120
The Endless Vearth!

244
00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:36.730
Where am I?

245
00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:39.600
[GAN FALL]
Inside the ruins of Shandora.

246
00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.230
[WYPER]
Gan Fall!

247
00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:44.360
You shouldn't move yet.

248
00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:46.610
[WYPER]
You! You're a Skypiean!

249
00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:50.710
[CHIEFTAIN]
Rest.

250
00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:52.090
[WYPER]
Chief!

251
00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.010
We are all bound together.

252
00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:56.600
Made brothers by the war.

253
00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:58.140
[WYPER]
The golden belfry.

254
00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:00.890
It's the Shandorians' sacred
duty to protect it to the end!

255
00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.950
[drumbeat]

256
00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:04.120
Listen.

257
00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:07.420
That's the sound of war
drums announcing battle!

258
00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:10.570
There's the signal fire, too!

259
00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:12.070
[CHIEFTAIN]
Patience, Wyper.

260
00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:13.630
Rest a while longer.

261
00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:16.400
The heroism of our ancestors is clear.

262
00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:22.230
But whatever violence happened in the past,
you must allow it to stay there.

263
00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:24.150
Our future starts here.

264
00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:27.790
This is our home now, and we
Shandorians will make it a good one.

265
00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:29.170
[GAN FALL]
Yes.

266
00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:32.710
Most often, the call for
vengeance cannot be ignored.

267
00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:38.630
But today, it has been drowned out by
a sea of voices screaming in celebration.

268
00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:40.640
[CROWD celebrating]

269
00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.890
[AISA laughs, cheers]

270
00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:52.410
We did it!

271
00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:54.040
Yes! Yes! Yes!

272
00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:55.660
[celebrating continues]

273
00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:07.620
All right!

274
00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:07.490
When you're lost and alone, call out and lead me to your side

275
00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:12.910
As you wander far from home, you search the sky and never hide

276
00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:15.710
You are so much like the moon

277
00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:20.360
Calmer than a star, your twinkling's lost

278
00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:32.760
A deep reflection shines, you slowly leave, fading, and what's the cost?

279
00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:37.990
Stay as you are, don't lose your way

280
00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:46.300
Let my words guide you, and look ahead until the day!

281
00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:53.190
Don't give up on your dreams, through endless nights they come to you

282
00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:58.810
If you stop, you'll never see them shining through!

283
00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:04.580
Will you return? Maybe not... Will you learn? I hope you do

284
00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:10.970
Please put your past to rest, and live your life anew.
